  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Temperatures will sink below seasonal norms for\nthe next several days. Freeze Watch in effect for most of the\narea late Saturday night into Sunday morning.\n\nLatest surface analysis shows a cold front well offshore of the\nCarolinas, with chilly high pressure well to the northwest. \nCooler and drier air has been seeping into the area over the\nlast few hours. Highs only get into the lower 60s this afternoon,\nsome 12-15 degrees cooler than yesterday. Even colder tonight, \nwith lows in the mid 30s inland, lower 40s at the coast. Can't\nrule out some isolated frost tonight in sheltered areas and\nrooftops. Despite that, it appears to be a tad too warm and\nbreezy for a Frost Advisory tonight.\n\nTemperatures continue to trend colder, with highs not even\nleaving the 50s this weekend. Freeze Watch from late Saturday\nnight through Sunday morning for the majority of northeast SC\nand southeast NC, sans the immediate coastline and all of New \nHanover County. Lows Saturday night dip down into the lower 30s\ninland, mid 30s at the coast.\n\nGoing into early next week, temperatures rebound slightly by a\ndegree or two Monday and Tuesday. More considerable air mass\nmodification kicks off Wednesday onward, with highs reaching the\n70s again by about Thursday. Frost is possible at night in the\nearlier half of the week. Forecast continues to look quite dry.",
